            "review_title": "Review at Banh Cuon Tay Ho",
            "review_text": "El V\n45 contributions\n1\nFresh and Tasty\nDec 2017 • Couples\nLiving close to Little Saigon in California, I have a lot of options for Vietnamese food. There are some restaurants that offer better Vietnamese food than in the Motherland because of the quality of ingredients overseas. Little Saigon has many bánh cuốn options, including some with the same name. None of those options come anywhere close to Bánh Cuốn Tây Hồ in Hồ Chí Minh city. The rice paper here is freshly made and paper thin (the sign of the best bánh cuốn according to my extremely Vietnamese mother). The filling is a mixture of minced pork, mushrooms, and onions. I'm salivating just thinking about it. Foreigners also do not need to worry because the restaurant has a set menu with listed prices. There's no foreigner \"tax\". Bánh cuốn is one of the truly Vietnamese dishes. Everyone should experience this flavor of Vietnam.\nRead more\nWritten December 29, 2017",
