            "review_text": "Christine D\nVancouver, Canada26 contributions\n0\nBeautiful Banh Cuon....\nMar 2016 • Family\nOne of Vietnamese's most favourite dishes, Banh means flower/bread, an con means roll. I wish we had more time here to really just let it all sink in. But alas, with our time restriction, it was quite good! The fish sauce could use a bit more life, but a fantastic place for Banh Cuon. Don't know the dish or scared of it? Don't sweat, nothing scary, just good ol' simple ground beef wrapped in a steamed rice flower sheet, but it is lifeless without the nuoc mam (Fish sauce) Yummy! Wikipedia: Banh Cuon.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 23, 2016",
